{
    "sample": "vis-network-specimen-mappings-bypass",
    "program": "vis-network",
    "version": "vis-network 9.1.9 (standalone), svgcanvas 2.6.0",
    "command": "new vis.Network(<div 1200x900>, { nodes: file.nodes, edges: file.edges }, file.options); net.renderer._redraw() onto an svgcanvas Context",
    "how": "vis-network draws with Canvas 2D only. At the snapshot point (observed.snapshotAt), its own CanvasRenderer._redraw ran once with net.canvas.getContext returning an svgcanvas context, so every draw call vis-network made (edges, nodes, arrows, labels) was recorded as SVG at the view vis-network itself chose. The svgcanvas context is corrected where it departs from a canvas (SVG_CONTEXT in web-oracle.mjs): the current path survives save() and fillText(), a text keeps its blanks (xml:space), a Path2D argument is replayed (with the paths added to it), a clip keeps its evenodd rule, gradients and 1-wide or dashed strokes follow the transform, and a text outline is not scaled twice; each was checked against Chromium's own screenshot of the same drawing. A shadow (shadowColor, shadowBlur, shadowOffsetX / Y) is recorded as an feDropShadow filter in device pixels. A destination-out stroke over the ring just stroked on the same path (a Cytoscape.js double border or outline) is recorded as a mask on that ring; no other globalCompositeOperation is recorded. Not recorded: a glyph the pinned fonts lack (a vis-network icon) rasterizes as a box where Chromium draws nothing.",
    "svgKind": "vector",
